WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.501
-The committee investigating

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.434
the attempted coup
on January 6th

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:06.267
has proven,
in painstaking detail,

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.467
that Donald Trump orchestrated
a premeditated plan

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.934
for overthrowing the government
on January 6th,

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:13.834
even though his closest aides
and advisors knew

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.734
his stolen election claims
were insane.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.701
In fact, it was all
such an obvious scam

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.968
that Trump campaign official
Kimberly Guilfoyle,

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.534
the fiancée of Donald Trump Jr.,

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.033
got paid an obscene amount
of money

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.200
for a speech that lasted less
than three minutes.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.300
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.100
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.167
The political world
is still processing

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.968
the aftermath of some
of the revelations

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.334
from the January 6th Committee's
second hearing on Monday.

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:41.434
For example, Rudy Giuliani,
wants you all to know

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:44.300
he is very upset
at the accusation leveled

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.701
by former Trump aides,
in sworn testimony,

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.601
that he was wasted
on election night.

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:52.400
-Former Trump lawyer
Rudy Giuliani has now responded

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.501
to those accusations in the
January 6th Committee hearings

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.767
that he was drunk
on election night,

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.934
Giuliani writing in part...

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.367
-Oh, sorry, buddy,
you just gave yourself away.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:20.167
No one's favorite drink is

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.133
Diet Pepsi.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.467
Is your favorite cookie
Lorna Doone's?

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.601
Diet Pepsi is what you drink
on a flight

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:30.033
when they don't have Diet Coke

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:31.667
or lemonade or chocolate milk

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.868
or coconut water or camel spit

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.133
or regular Pepsi.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.300
If a waiter ever says,
"We don't have Diet Coke.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.300
Is Diet Pepsi okay?",
you're legally allowed

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.534
to stab them with a fork.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.334
Maybe Rudy has an unpopular
favorite drink on purpose,

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:47.501
you know, so he has a cover
story when he's at a bar.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.000
[ As Giuliani ]
I'll take a Diet Pepsi.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.501
"Oh, we don't have that, sir."
[ As Giuliani ] That's too bad.

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:51.601
In that case, I'll have, uh,

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.133
16 ounces of scotch
in a watering can.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:55.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.334
Also, what do you mean,

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.067
you refused
all alcohol that evening?

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:02.901
Like people were trying
to get you to drink,

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:05.601
[ Laughter ]
but you said no.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.300
Feels like you're being
a little too defensive.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.534
You sound like me coming home
at 2:00 am in high school.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:14.234
[ Posh accent ]
No, Mom, I'm sober as a judge!

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.067
[ Laughter ]
Oh, they tried
to get me to drink,

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:18.133
but I said nay, I will not

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.634
[ Laughter ]
sully the good Meyers name

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.367
with the demon taste
of Jagermeister.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:23.801
Oh, no, no.
I'm going to barf.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.300
Move, Mom.
Move.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.868
I doubt anyone was trying
to get Rudy drunk,

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:32.767
although, I could definitely see
Trump aides, on election night,

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:35.200
trying to overserve him,
just so he passes out.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.267
"We're all upset about Arizona,
Mr. Mayor.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:39.667
You know what?
Why don't you drink this

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:42.000
and then go lie down
on the lawn outside?"

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.434
Because, according to the sworn
testimony obtained

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.467
by the committee,
Rudy was just wandering

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.934
around the White House
on election night,

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.267
looking for the president,

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:53.434
so we could tell him
to declare the election stolen.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.234
-Do you remember
Rudy Giuliani being

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:57.267
at the White House
on election night

00:02:57.267 --> 00:03:00.067
and into the early hours
the next morning?

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.601
-I do.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.300
What do you remember
about when he came?

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:08.033
-Um...
[ Clears throat ]

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.200
He...

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.667
He was, um...

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.100
[ Laughter ]
They were -- I had heard

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.734
that he was, uh,
upstairs, you know,

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:20.000
in that aforementioned
reception area,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.567
and...um,

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.367
he was looking
to talk to the president.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.501
-You know, you like to think
of the White House

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.167
as a stately, dignified place,
full of decorum and history,

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:32.100
and then you learn,
via congressional testimony,

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.167
that a drunken potato goblin
was upstairs,

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.334
[ Laughter ]
just wandering around all night,

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:37.801
banging on doors,

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.067
looking, not just for anyone,
but the president,

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.734
and, by the way, got to him.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.200
[ As Giuliani ]
Excuse me, sir.
Do you happen to know

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.801
where Donald is?
I need to talk to him.

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:48.701
"Mr. Mayor, that's just a bust
of Abraham Lincoln."

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:49.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:50.968
[ As Giuliani ]
He's a bust, all right.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.701
He won't even give me
my Diet Pepsi.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.434
[ Laughter ]
And, by the way,

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:55.868
it's worth underscoring
this point --

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.667
it's not Democrats saying
Rudy was drunk

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.100
at the White House
on election night.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.467
It's his fellow
Trump supporters,

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:03.200
like former Trump campaign
spokesman Jason Miller.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.834
-Was there anyone in that
conversation who,

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:08.968
in your observation,
had had too much to drink?

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.400
[ Laughter ]
-Tell me more about that.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.734
What was your observation
about his, uh,

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:21.767
potential intoxication
during that -- that discussion

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:25.033
about what the president
should say

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.200
when he addressed the nation
on election night.

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:40.634
-I mean, I think we can guess
at his level of intoxication.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:41.801
I mean, look at him.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.167
[ Laughter ]
For a guy Rudy Giuliani's age,

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:46.100
there's very little room
between stone-cold sober

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.767
and sloshed out of his
[bleep] mind.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.968
[ Laughter ]
It's a little like
when your grandma

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:52.267
has one glass of wine
with an ice cube in it

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:54.334
when you're out to dinner
and she starts telling you

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:57.200
what an [bleep] your father
was as a baby.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.167
So, Rudy may have been drunk
on election night,

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:00.667
according to former
Trump advisors,

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.868
but his suggestion

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.868
that Trump just declare
the election stolen

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.968
was not some random,
drunken impulse.

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.634
As the committee documented,

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:09.467
Trump had been openly declaring,

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:10.968
for months
in advance of the election,

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:13.567
that the only way he could lose
was if it was stolen from him.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:16.467
He was just desperately
searching for any pretext,

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.667
any justification at all,
that he could use

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:20.567
to make that declaration
and Rudy,

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:23.200
along with a gang of other
crazy weirdos, gave it to him.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.767
In fact, Trump officials
kept telling him,

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:27.000
over and over and over again,
that each individual claim

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.334
of election fraud was nonsense
and, rather than push back

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.200
and offer his own evidence
for each claim,

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.200
Trump would just move on
to some other insane claim.

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:48.501
that much of the information
he's getting is false...

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:05.367
-I told him that the stuff
that his people were shoveling

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:07.868
out to the public was bullshit.

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:10.567
I mean, that the claims
of fraud were bullshit.

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:13.300
-Quick tangent -- when Bill Barr
says bull[bleep] in the clip,

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.033
we don't have to bleep it,
but when I repeat him, we do.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:18.534
[ Laughter ]
That's where we're at,
as a nation.

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:21.968
I'm not allowed to say a word,
on my show,

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:24.901
but Donald Trump's
former attorney general is.

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:25.868
That's some bull[bleep].

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:28.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.067
But that testimony
is also revealing.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:31.834
Trump kept pitching insane ideas

00:06:31.834 --> 00:06:33.200
and then,
when they were challenged,

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.100
instead of trying to provide
evidence for those claims,

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.400
he just moved on
to the next one.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.634
He was like a kid trying
to explain to his teacher

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:39.701
why he didn't do his homework.

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:40.868
"Uh, dog ate it."

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:41.734
You don't have a dog.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.234
"It was someone else's dog.

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:45.033
It broke into my house.
It ate my homework.

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:47.467
And yet, instead of tracking
down this criminal canine,
you're grilling me

00:06:47.467 --> 00:06:49.501
about my "Tale of Two Cities"
book report? That's some...

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:50.534
-Bull[bleep].

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:51.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.534
-Interesting --
we had to beep it that time

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.501
because it wasn't us
repeating the news.

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:58.434
It was us using him
to make a punchline of a joke.

00:06:58.434 --> 00:07:00.400
[ Laughter ]
So, when we use it as a joke,
we have to beep it,

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.767
but when it's newsworthy,

00:07:01.767 --> 00:07:04.133
we're allowed to do it
the way it was said.

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:06.968
And I think explaining it
the way I'm doing it

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:08.300
is newsworthy.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.501 --> 00:07:13.968
[ Applause ]

00:07:13.968 --> 00:07:15.601
Which I think is [bleep] cool?

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:16.901
Let's find out.

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:17.834
[ Laughter and applause ]
Let's watch tonight.

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:19.133
Let's watch tonight.

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:20.501
I think I was making news.

00:07:22.701 --> 00:07:25.300
Ooh! I know what --
If Bill Barr gets a talk show,

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:26.934
he can show what I just did.

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:29.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.300
Again, that testimony,
in particular, is so important

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.868
because it establishes that
Trump knew what he was doing.

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:38.367
He had criminal intent.

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:40.133
It was a plan, not a whim.

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:42.467
He and his cronies want you
to think January 6th

00:07:42.467 --> 00:07:43.868
was just some random,
one-off event

00:07:43.868 --> 00:07:45.400
that was neither preplanned

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.100
nor part of a broader attempt
to overthrow the government.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.834
For example,
Rudy has a podcast --

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:53.133
because I guess
that's what they give you now,

00:07:53.133 --> 00:07:55.200
instead of meds -- where
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.334
he reacted to the first
committee hearing

00:07:57.334 --> 00:07:59.634
by claiming the FBI
had found no evidence

00:07:59.634 --> 00:08:01.801
of preplanning
for the January 6th attack.

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:05.267
-They have become,
not just an embarrassment.

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:08.400
They've become a danger
to the freedom of Americans.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.968
The FBI, in its investigation,
found no such structure.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.000
They found that --

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.234
pretty shortly after,
they found that there was

00:08:17.234 --> 00:08:21.667
no evidence of preplanning
of this event.

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.601
So, then you'd have to say

00:08:23.601 --> 00:08:26.133
it was some kind
of a spontaneous --

00:08:26.133 --> 00:08:28.467
And I think, by this time,
we're all quite convinced, now,

00:08:28.467 --> 00:08:31.200
that it's not a -- uh,

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.300
it's not an insurrection.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.601
It's a -- It's a riot.

00:08:33.601 --> 00:08:38.834
And -- And -- And one that,
according to the FBI,

00:08:38.834 --> 00:08:42.067
on several occasions,
was not preplanned.

00:08:42.067 --> 00:08:43.501
-Alright, first of all,
the Justice Department

00:08:43.501 --> 00:08:44.934
has already charged
multiple members

00:08:44.934 --> 00:08:46.567
of militias
and other right-wing groups

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:48.400
with seditious conspiracy,
so that's wrong.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.501
Second, how the [bleep]
does Rudy

00:08:50.501 --> 00:08:52.868
have more than one camera
set up? I mean...

00:08:52.868 --> 00:08:54.367
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:56.601
[ Fresh laughter and applause ]

00:08:56.601 --> 00:08:57.968
...I did --

00:08:57.968 --> 00:09:02.567
You guys, I did an actual
network television show

00:09:02.567 --> 00:09:04.501
by myself, in my house,
for a year.

00:09:04.501 --> 00:09:07.300
All I had was an iPad
and a ring light.

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.234
And then everyone in the YouTube
comment section

00:09:09.234 --> 00:09:10.701
was saying mean things
to me, like,

00:09:10.701 --> 00:09:13.033
"Is this show hosted
by Tintin's ghost?"

00:09:13.033 --> 00:09:15.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:18.701 --> 00:09:20.767
I would've killed
for a second camera

00:09:20.767 --> 00:09:22.901
or a cool leather chair
like that.

00:09:22.901 --> 00:09:24.501
[ Laughter ]
Rudy's supposed to be

00:09:24.501 --> 00:09:26.434
the drunk, crazy person trying
to overthrow the government.

00:09:26.434 --> 00:09:28.701
Meanwhile, he's got
a multicam setup in his office,

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:30.033
with a desk and a leather chair

00:09:30.033 --> 00:09:31.934
and I was the one with my hair
down to my shoulders,

00:09:31.934 --> 00:09:34.534
talking to a [bleep] painting
of a Sea Captain.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:35.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:35.434 --> 00:09:37.267
By the way, if you're wondering

00:09:37.267 --> 00:09:38.634
where the Sea Captain went,

00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:40.968
he ran into a little
legal trouble.

00:09:40.968 --> 00:09:42.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:42.901 --> 00:09:45.934
I told him to get off 4chan,
but he wouldn't listen!

00:09:45.934 --> 00:09:47.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:48.868
Also, I want to go back to this.

00:09:48.868 --> 00:09:51.367
-They have become,
not just an embarrassment.

00:09:52.334 --> 00:09:55.234
They've become a danger
to the freedom of Americans.

00:09:55.234 --> 00:09:57.334
-You really want to call
anyone else an embarrassment?

00:09:57.334 --> 00:09:59.100
Is that really the word
you want to use?

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:00.868
[ Laughter ]
There was an entire
nationally televised

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:02.300
congressional hearing,
this week,

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.734
about you being a sloppy drunk.

00:10:03.734 --> 00:10:05.200
[ Laughter ]
You used to be
on magazine covers,

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.367
as America's Mayor,
and now, you're most famous

00:10:07.367 --> 00:10:09.868
for screaming
outside a landscaping company,

00:10:09.868 --> 00:10:12.667
like a guy who was trying
to return a used bag of mulch.

00:10:12.667 --> 00:10:14.334
[ Laughter ]
[ As Giuliani ]
So what if I already put it?

00:10:14.334 --> 00:10:16.234
Yeah, yeah, what if I already
put the mulch down and I

00:10:16.234 --> 00:10:18.033
decided I don't want any more,
so I scooped it all back up

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:19.667
and I put it back in the bag?
And no, you cannot

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:21.868
hold me responsible
if there's a dog turd in there.

00:10:21.868 --> 00:10:23.033
[ Laughter ]
If you should blame anyone,

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:25.167
it's the dog who broke
into my house!

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:26.501
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.501 --> 00:10:29.133
So, they knew the allegations
of fraud were all insane.

00:10:29.133 --> 00:10:31.367
It was a scam.
And there's really

00:10:31.367 --> 00:10:33.701
no better proof
of the fact that it was a scam

00:10:33.701 --> 00:10:35.133
than this detail, revealed

00:10:35.133 --> 00:10:36.334
by one of the members
of the committee.

00:10:36.334 --> 00:10:38.734
Trump campaign official
Kimberly Guilfoyle,

00:10:38.734 --> 00:10:40.634
who is also
Donald Trump Jr.'s fiancée,

00:10:40.634 --> 00:10:43.767
was paid an absolutely grotesque
amount of money

00:10:43.767 --> 00:10:45.501
for her speech
on the day of the insurrection,

00:10:45.501 --> 00:10:48.133
a speech that lasted less
than three minutes.

00:10:48.133 --> 00:10:49.934
-The committee
has found information

00:10:49.934 --> 00:10:51.534
that Kimberly Guilfoyle

00:10:51.534 --> 00:10:54.033
was paid $60,000

00:10:54.033 --> 00:10:56.901
to speak at the rally
on January 6th,

00:10:56.901 --> 00:10:59.334
$60,000 for a speech that was,
what, three minutes?

00:10:59.334 --> 00:11:01.601
-If that.
-If that. Three minutes long.

00:11:01.601 --> 00:11:05.033
And what have you heard,
over the last several hours,

00:11:05.033 --> 00:11:06.801
since that revelation,

00:11:06.801 --> 00:11:09.067
about how people
in Trumpworld feel about this?

00:11:09.067 --> 00:11:10.667
-So, I want to say two things
about that.

00:11:10.667 --> 00:11:13.267
People in Trumpworld
are sharing that clip.

00:11:13.267 --> 00:11:15.501
They are aghast that this is
the amount of money

00:11:15.501 --> 00:11:18.934
that she got for a speech
to introduce her boyfriend.

00:11:18.934 --> 00:11:22.334
-$60,000 for a speech that was
less than three minutes long,

00:11:22.334 --> 00:11:23.734
and to introduce her fiancée.

00:11:23.734 --> 00:11:26.434
If there was ever a man
who needed no introduction,

00:11:26.434 --> 00:11:30.400
[ Laughter ]
it's Don Jr. at a far-right
conservative rally.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:32.834
That's like going up
at a "Star Trek" convention

00:11:32.834 --> 00:11:34.567
to introduce William Shatner.

00:11:34.567 --> 00:11:36.801
Uh, they know him.

00:11:36.801 --> 00:11:38.100
[ Laughter ]

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.067
[ Transatlantic accent ]
Many years ago, a starship

00:11:40.067 --> 00:11:42.367
set out on a five-year mission.

00:11:42.367 --> 00:11:44.567
"Move, or we'll kill you!"

00:11:44.567 --> 00:11:46.934
[ Laughter ]
By the way,

00:11:46.934 --> 00:11:49.234
now, I guess we know
what she really meant

00:11:49.234 --> 00:11:51.801
when she said this at the RNC
in 2020 --

00:11:51.801 --> 00:11:54.367
-The best is yet

00:11:54.367 --> 00:11:55.701
to come!

00:11:55.701 --> 00:11:57.234
-$5,200.

00:11:57.234 --> 00:12:00.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:02.234 --> 00:12:03.701
-Also, if she genuinely thought

00:12:03.701 --> 00:12:06.400
this was a revolution
to save America from tyranny,

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.200
then why was she getting paid
at all?

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.033
It's not a corporate
speaking gig

00:12:10.033 --> 00:12:11.467
where you charge
your standard rate.

00:12:11.467 --> 00:12:14.701
You think Paul Revere got paid
for his midnight ride?

00:12:14.701 --> 00:12:16.067
[ Laughter ]
[ New York accent ]
"I need to bring the lights.

00:12:16.067 --> 00:12:18.300
I got to remember my lines.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.267
You're making me
use my own horse."

00:12:21.267 --> 00:12:22.400
Who can forget his famous quote?

00:12:25.901 --> 00:12:27.100
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.167
The committee has proven,
in exhaustive detail,

00:12:30.167 --> 00:12:32.767
not just that Trump's
stolen election claims were BS,

00:12:32.767 --> 00:12:34.200
but he knew they were BS
and virtually

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.033
everyone around him told him
they were BS.

00:12:36.033 --> 00:12:38.234
They were both a scam
to raise money

00:12:38.234 --> 00:12:40.534
and a fabricated pretext
for an attempted coup,

00:12:40.534 --> 00:12:43.467
a coup orchestrated, in part,
by Rudy Giuliani,

00:12:43.467 --> 00:12:46.400
whose blood alcohol level
on election night was roughly...

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.501
-60,000.

00:12:47.501 --> 00:12:49.767
[ Laughter ]

00:12:49.767 --> 00:12:51.234
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:51.234 --> 00:12:54.901
♪♪

